  "icon": "switch",
  "color": "#64748b",
  "sourceUrl": "https://www.downloads.netgear.com/files/GDC/M4250/M4250_Datasheet.pdf",
  "fabric": {
    "capacityMbps": 240000,
    "kind": "switching fabric",
    "note": "Vendor 240 Gbps non-blocking fabric across 48 ports (40 x 1G + 8 x 10G = 120 Gbit/s each way); forwarding rate 178.56 Mpps, line rate."
  },
  "poe": {
    "budgetW": 2880,
    "sourceUrl": "https://www.downloads.netgear.com/files/GDC/M4250/M4250_Datasheet.pdf",
    "note": "2,880 W only with all three internal power supplies connected: the datasheet states 720 W on one PSU, 1,650 W on two and 2,880 W on three. The 40 port ceilings sum to 40 x 90 W = 3,600 W, so even a fully-fed chassis cannot run 40 Ultra90 ports at 90 W; at 2,880 W the average is 72 W per port."
  },
  "notes": "M4250 series common platform: 16K MAC addresses, 4K ARP/NDP entries, 4K VLANs, static routes (894 IPv4 / 126 IPv6) plus RIP (32 IPv4), DHCP server (2K leases), sFlow, SNMP, console/telnet/SSH CLI and the AV web GUI. The only 2U M4250 and the only one with three fixed C14 inlets. Port census matches the M4250-40G8XF-PoE+ (40 PoE + 8 SFP+), so the model string carries the SKU to keep the two catalogue keys apart. Ultra90 802.3bt PSEs are backward compatible with 802.3af/at per the datasheet footnote. Sources: datasheet https://www.downloads.netgear.com/files/GDC/M4250/M4250_Datasheet.pdf and https://kb.netgear.com/000064904/NETGEAR-AV-Line-of-Fully-Managed-Switches-M4250-Series."
}
